---
title: Gallery
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /gallery/
---
<h1 class="page-title">Gallery</h1>

{% if gallery.length %}
{#- Per-tree progression filter. A button + listbox rather than a
    <select>, because the native control's popup is drawn by the browser:
    its highlight is the OS accent (blue in Chrome, grey in Edge) with no
    way to reach it from CSS, and on Android it opens as a full-screen
    dialog. This one is ours, so it follows the theme on every platform.
    gallery.js fills the options from the manifest's `trees` arrays and
    unhides the control; with no `trees` values (or without JS) the full
    gallery just shows as-is. #}
<div class="gallery-filter" hidden>
  <div class="tree-filter">
    <span class="visually-hidden" id="tree-filter-hint">Filter photos by tree:</span>
    <button type="button" class="tree-filter-button" id="tree-filter-button"
            aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="tree-filter-list"
            aria-labelledby="tree-filter-hint tree-filter-value">
      <span class="tree-filter-value" id="tree-filter-value">All trees</span>
      <svg class="tree-filter-chevron" width="12" height="8" viewBox="0 0 12 8"
           aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M1 1.5l5 5 5-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
    </button>
    <ul class="tree-filter-list" id="tree-filter-list" role="listbox"
        aria-label="Filter photos by tree" hidden></ul>
  </div>
</div>

{#- The card's href is the full-size original on the CDN — what the
    lightbox opens, and what a visitor gets with JavaScript off. The <img>
    inside it is a build-cut thumbnail; see galleryThumb in
    eleventy.config.js for why the two are not the same file. #}
<div id="gallery" class="gallery-grid">
  {%- for item in gallery %}
  <a class="gallery-card" href="{{ site.images.cdn }}{{ item.file }}">
    <div class="cdn-frame" style="aspect-ratio: {{ item.ratio or "3/4" }}">
      {% galleryThumb item, loop.index0 %}
    </div>
    <div class="gallery-card-caption">
      <div class="gallery-card-species">{{ item.species }}</div>
      <div class="gallery-card-meta">{{ item.style }} · {{ item.date }}</div>
    </div>
  </a>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>

{#- The grid shows a batch at a time once the gallery outgrows one.
    Every card is in the HTML either way — a hidden card costs no image
    bytes, because a browser does not fetch a lazy <img> it is not
    displaying — so this is gallery.js revealing what is already here,
    not fetching more. Without JavaScript nothing is hidden and the whole
    gallery is there, which is the one thing paginated pages could not do.
    The control ships hidden and gallery.js unhides it, the same bargain
    the tree filter and the theme toggle make. #}
<div class="gallery-more" hidden>
  <button type="button" class="gallery-more-button">Show more</button>
  <p class="gallery-more-count" role="status"></p>
</div>

{# Item metadata (ratio, notes, …) for the lightbox, so gallery.js never
   has to re-fetch the manifest. "</" is escaped so notes text can never
   close this script block. #}
<script type="application/json" id="gallery-data">{{ gallery | dump | replace("</", "<\\/") | safe }}</script>
<script src="/assets/js/gallery.js" defer></script>
{% else %}
<p class="gallery-status">The gallery couldn’t be loaded when this version
of the site was built — it will be back with the next deploy.</p>
{% endif %}
